Fixed. The change in gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/stream/JsonWriter.java:495 makes `value(double)` respect lenient mode, matching `value(Number)`:

```java
if (!lenient && (Double.isNaN(value) || Double.isInfinite(value))) {
  throw new IllegalArgumentException("Numeric values must be finite, but was " + value);
}
```

The write path already handles NaN/Infinity correctly (`JsonScope.numberLiteral` via `LazilyParsedNumber` emits them unquoted), so no other change was needed. I also added a `@throws` javadoc noting the lenient-mode behavior.

Verification:
- `JsonWriterTest`: all 39 tests pass
- Full test suite: the only failures (7F/4E in `DefaultDateTypeAdapterTest`, `DefaultTypeAdaptersTest`, `ObjectTest`) are pre-existing on the unmodified tree — they're locale-dependent date tests unrelated to this change
